{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Calibri;}}\fs22 \par\b\fs32 Accessibility Conformance Report\b0\fs22\par \par WCAG Edition  \par Based on VPAT Version 2.5\par \par \par\b\fs28 Product Information\b0\fs22\par \par Name of Product / Version: Demo Web Shop - Playwright POM Accessibility Assessment  \par Report Date: May 21, 2026  \par Product URL Evaluated: https://demowebshop.tricentis.com/  \par Contact Information: Project QA / Accessibility Test Owner  \par Report Type: Draft Accessibility Conformance Report based on automated test findings\par \par \par\b\fs28 Notes\b0\fs22\par \par This Accessibility Conformance Report is prepared in the VPAT 2.5 WCAG Edition style. The assessment was limited to automated Playwright tests using @axe-core/playwright and axe WCAG 2.0 A / AA rule tags. Manual testing with screen readers, keyboard-only navigation, browser zoom/reflow, voice control, and cognitive accessibility checks was not performed.\par \par Because the tested site is an external demo application, this report documents observed conformance issues and remediation recommendations. It should not be treated as a final vendor VPAT certification.\par \par \par\b\fs28 Evaluation Methods Used\b0\fs22\par \par      Method      Details     \par      ---      ---     \par      Automated testing      Playwright accessibility spec using `@axe-core/playwright`     \par      Test command      `npm run test:a11y`     \par      Browser project      `chromium`     \par      Blocking impacts      axe `critical` and `serious`     \par      Pages / flows tested      Homepage, Login, Register, Product Search, Cart, Checkout     \par      Output artifacts      `results.xml`, `playwright-report/`, `allure-results/`, `allure-report/`     \par      Test result      6 failed / 6 executed     \par \par \par\b\fs28 Applicable Standards / Guidelines\b0\fs22\par \par      Standard / Guideline      Included in Report     \par      ---      ---     \par      Web Content Accessibility Guidelines 2.0 Level A      Yes     \par      Web Content Accessibility Guidelines 2.0 Level AA      Yes     \par      Revised Section 508      Referenced through WCAG A / AA mapping     \par \par \par\b\fs28 Terms\b0\fs22\par \par      Term      Definition Used in This Report     \par      ---      ---     \par      Supports      The tested functionality has no known defect for the criterion based on available evidence.     \par      Partially Supports      Some functionality meets the criterion, but one or more tested areas have defects.     \par      Does Not Support      The majority of tested functionality related to the criterion does not meet the requirement.     \par      Not Applicable      The criterion is not relevant to the evaluated product or tested scope.     \par      Not Evaluated      The criterion was not evaluated in this automated-only assessment.     \par \par \par\b\fs28 Executive Summary\b0\fs22\par \par The automated accessibility suite found critical or serious violations on every tested page. The evaluated site currently does not support several WCAG Level A and Level AA criteria that are relevant to Revised Section 508 conformance.\par \par Primary blocking issues:\par \par      Issue      Impact      Affected Pages     \par      ---      ---      ---     \par      Missing page language      Serious      Homepage, Login, Register, Product Search, Cart, Checkout     \par      Form controls without accessible labels      Critical      Homepage, Login, Register, Product Search, Cart, Checkout     \par      Select controls without accessible names      Critical      Product Search     \par      Image without alternative text      Critical      Homepage     \par      Link without discernible text      Serious      Homepage     \par      Insufficient text contrast      Serious      Checkout     \par \par \par\b\fs28 Table 1: Success Criteria, Level A\b0\fs22\par \par      Criteria      Conformance Level      Remarks and Explanations     \par      ---      ---      ---     \par      1.1.1 Non-text Content      Does Not Support      Homepage fails axe `image-alt` for `.nivo-main-image`. Informative images require meaningful alternative text; decorative images require empty `alt=""`.     \par      1.2.1 Audio-only and Video-only (Prerecorded)      Not Applicable      No audio-only or video-only content was included in the tested e-commerce pages.     \par      1.2.2 Captions (Prerecorded)      Not Applicable      No prerecorded video with audio was included in the tested pages.     \par      1.2.3 Audio Description or Media Alternative (Prerecorded)      Not Applicable      No prerecorded video content was included in the tested pages.     \par      1.3.1 Info and Relationships      Not Evaluated      Automated findings did not include this criterion. Manual review of headings, lists, form groups, tables, and relationships is required.     \par      1.3.2 Meaningful Sequence      Not Evaluated      Manual keyboard and screen reader reading order validation is required.     \par      1.3.3 Sensory Characteristics      Not Evaluated      Manual review is required to confirm instructions do not depend only on shape, size, position, orientation, or sound.     \par      1.4.1 Use of Color      Not Evaluated      Manual review is required to confirm color is not the only means of conveying information.     \par      1.4.2 Audio Control      Not Applicable      No auto-playing audio was observed in the automated test scope.     \par      2.1.1 Keyboard      Not Evaluated      Manual keyboard-only testing is required for all page flows.     \par      2.1.2 No Keyboard Trap      Not Evaluated      Manual keyboard-only testing is required to confirm focus can enter and leave all components.     \par      2.1.4 Character Key Shortcuts      Not Evaluated      No shortcut-key review was performed.     \par      2.2.1 Timing Adjustable      Not Evaluated      Timeout and session behavior were not evaluated.     \par      2.2.2 Pause, Stop, Hide      Not Evaluated      Moving slider behavior on the homepage should be manually reviewed for pause, stop, or hide controls.     \par      2.3.1 Three Flashes or Below Threshold      Not Evaluated      Flashing content was not manually evaluated.     \par      2.4.1 Bypass Blocks      Not Evaluated      Skip links, landmarks, and bypass mechanisms were not manually evaluated.     \par      2.4.2 Page Titled      Not Evaluated      Page titles were not included in the automated finding set. Manual review is required.     \par      2.4.3 Focus Order      Not Evaluated      Manual keyboard focus-order testing is required.     \par      2.4.4 Link Purpose (In Context)      Does Not Support      Homepage fails axe `link-name` for `.nivo-imageLink:nth-child(1)`. The slider link needs visible text, hidden accessible text, or an `aria-label` that communicates purpose.     \par      2.5.1 Pointer Gestures      Not Evaluated      Pointer gesture behavior was not manually evaluated.     \par      2.5.2 Pointer Cancellation      Not Evaluated      Pointer cancellation behavior was not manually evaluated.     \par      2.5.3 Label in Name      Not Evaluated      Manual review is required to confirm visible labels are included in accessible names.     \par      2.5.4 Motion Actuation      Not Applicable      No motion-actuated functionality was observed in the automated test scope.     \par      3.1.1 Language of Page      Does Not Support      All tested pages fail axe `html-has-lang`; the root `html` element must include a valid language attribute such as `lang="en"`.     \par      3.2.1 On Focus      Not Evaluated      Manual interaction testing is required to confirm focus does not trigger unexpected context changes.     \par      3.2.2 On Input      Not Evaluated      Manual interaction testing is required to confirm input changes do not trigger unexpected context changes.     \par      3.3.1 Error Identification      Not Evaluated      Error validation flows were not evaluated in the automated accessibility run.     \par      3.3.2 Labels or Instructions      Does Not Support      All tested pages fail axe `label` for one or more form controls. Product Search also fails `select-name` for `#products-viewmode`, `#products-orderby`, and `#products-pagesize`.     \par      4.1.1 Parsing      Supports      WCAG 2.0 / 2.1 errata indicate this criterion is always considered supported unless using older reporting expectations. No automated parsing failure was reported.     \par      4.1.2 Name, Role, Value      Does Not Support      Form controls and selects without accessible names fail axe `label` and `select-name`. The homepage slider link also lacks a discernible accessible name.     \par \par \par\b\fs28 Table 2: Success Criteria, Level AA\b0\fs22\par \par      Criteria      Conformance Level      Remarks and Explanations     \par      ---      ---      ---     \par      1.2.4 Captions (Live)      Not Applicable      No live audio or video content was included in the tested scope.     \par      1.2.5 Audio Description (Prerecorded)      Not Applicable      No prerecorded video content was included in the tested scope.     \par      1.3.4 Orientation      Not Evaluated      Orientation behavior was not manually evaluated.     \par      1.3.5 Identify Input Purpose      Not Evaluated      Input purpose and autocomplete attributes were not evaluated manually.     \par      1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum)      Does Not Support      Checkout fails axe `color-contrast` for five checkout step headings: shipping, shipping method, payment method, payment information, and confirm order.     \par      1.4.4 Resize Text      Not Evaluated      Browser zoom and text resize testing were not performed.     \par      1.4.5 Images of Text      Not Evaluated      Manual review is required to confirm images of text are not used or have accessible alternatives.     \par      1.4.10 Reflow      Not Evaluated      Reflow at 320 CSS pixels was not tested.     \par      1.4.11 Non-text Contrast      Not Evaluated      Non-text component contrast was not manually evaluated.     \par      1.4.12 Text Spacing      Not Evaluated      Text spacing override testing was not performed.     \par      1.4.13 Content on Hover or Focus      Not Evaluated      Hover/focus-triggered content was not manually evaluated.     \par      2.4.5 Multiple Ways      Not Evaluated      Multiple navigation methods were not manually evaluated.     \par      2.4.6 Headings and Labels      Partially Supports      No automated heading or label text quality failures were reported, but form labeling failures indicate labels are incomplete across tested pages. Manual review is required.     \par      2.4.7 Focus Visible      Not Evaluated      Focus indicator visibility was not manually tested.     \par      3.1.2 Language of Parts      Not Evaluated      Language changes within page content were not evaluated.     \par      3.2.3 Consistent Navigation      Not Evaluated      Consistent navigation was not manually evaluated.     \par      3.2.4 Consistent Identification      Not Evaluated      Consistent identification of repeated controls was not manually evaluated.     \par      3.3.3 Error Suggestion      Not Evaluated      Error suggestion behavior was not evaluated.     \par      3.3.4 Error Prevention (Legal, Financial, Data)      Not Evaluated      Checkout/order error prevention behavior was not evaluated.     \par      4.1.3 Status Messages      Not Evaluated      Status message behavior was not evaluated with assistive technology.     \par \par \par\b\fs28 Section 508 Findings Summary\b0\fs22\par \par      Revised Section 508 Requirement Area      Conformance Level      Remarks     \par      ---      ---      ---     \par      302.1 Without Vision      Partially Supports      Automated findings indicate missing labels, missing language declaration, and missing link/image accessible names that affect screen reader users.     \par      302.2